// PSS v3.0 LRM — Example 60: Individual action handle array element traversal (page 134)
action A {
  rand bit[3:0]   f1;
}
action B {
  A a1, a2;

  activity {
    a1;
    a2 with {
      f1 < 10;
    };
  }
}
action C {
  action bit[3:0] max;
  B b1;

  activity {
    max;
    b1 with {
      a1.f1 <= max;
    };
  }
}
component pss_top {
    action A { }
    action entry {
        A   a_arr[4];
        A   a1, a2, a3, a4;
        activity {
            a_arr[0];
            a1;
        }
    }
}

When an action handle array is traversed as a whole, each array element is traversed independently
according to the semantics of the containing scope.
Example 61 below shows an action that traverses the elements of the a_arr action handle array in two
ways, depending on the value of a rand action attribute. Both ways of traversing the elements of a_arr
have identical semantics.
